\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 OVERVIEW
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 ========
\par 
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 This package contains C software to implement JPEG image compression and
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 decompression.  JPEG (pronounced "jay-peg") is a standardized compression
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 method f\hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 or full-color and gray-scale images.  JPEG is intended for compressing
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 "real-world" scenes; line drawings, cartoons and other non-realistic images
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 are not its strong suit.  JPEG is lossy, meaning that the output image is not
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 exactly identical to the input image.  Hence you must not use JPEG if you
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 have to have identical output bits.  However, on typical photographic images,
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 very good compression levels can be obtained with no visible change, and
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 remarkably high compression levels are possible if you can tol\hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 erate a
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 low-quality image.  For more details, see the references, or just experiment
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 with various compression settings.
\par 
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 This software implements JPEG baseline, extended-sequential, and progressive
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 compression processes.  Provision is made for supporting all variants of these
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 processes, although some uncommon parameter settings aren't implemented yet.
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 For legal reasons, we are not distributing code for the arithmetic-coding
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 variants of JPEG; see LEGAL ISSUES.  We have made no provision for supporting
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 the hierarchical or lossless processes defined in the standard.
\par 
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 We provide a set of library routines for reading and writing J\hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 PEG image files,
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 plus two sample applications "cjpeg" and "djpeg", which use the library to
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 perform conversion between JPEG and some other popular image file formats.
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 The library is intended to be reused in other applications.
\par 
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 In order to support file conversion and viewing software, we have included
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 considerable functionality beyond the bare JPEG coding/decoding capability;
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 for example, the color quantization modules are not strictly part of JPEG
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 decoding, but they are essential for output to colormapped \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 file formats or
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 colormapped displays.  These extra functions can be compiled out of the
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 library if not required for a particular application.  We have also included
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 "jpegtran", a utility for lossless transcoding between different JPEG
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 processes, and "rdjpgcom" and "wrjpgcom", two simple applications for
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 inserting and extracting textual comments in JFIF files.
\par 
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 The emphasis in designing this software has been on achieving portability and
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 flexibility, while also making it fast enough to be useful.  In particu\hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 lar,
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 the software is not intended to be read as a tutorial on JPEG.  (See the
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 REFERENCES section for introductory material.)  Rather, it is intended to
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 be reliable, portable, industrial-strength code.  We do not claim to have
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 achieved that goal in every aspect of the software, but we strive for it.
\par 
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 We welcome the use of this software as a component of commercial products.
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 No royalty is required, but we do ask for an acknowledgement in product
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 documentation, as described under LEGAL ISSUES.
