\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 It appears that the arithmetic coding option of the JPEG spec is covered by
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 patents owned by IBM, AT&T, and Mitsu\hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 bishi.  Hence arithmetic coding cannot
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 legally be used without obtaining one or more licenses.  For this reason,
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 support for arithmetic coding has been removed from the free JPEG software.
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 (Since arithmetic coding provides only a marginal gain over the unpatented
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 Huffman mode, it is unlikely that very many implementations will support it.)
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 So far as we are aware, there are no patent restrictions on the remaining
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 code.
\par 
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 The IJG distribution formerly included code to read and write GIF files.
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 To avoid entangl\hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 ement with the Unisys LZW patent, GIF reading support has
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 been removed altogether, and the GIF writer has been simplified to produce
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 "uncompressed GIFs".  This technique does not use the LZW algorithm; the
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 resulting GIF files are larger than usual, but are readable by all standard
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 GIF decoders.
