\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 REFERENCES
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 ==========
\par 
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 We highly recommend reading one or more of these references before trying to
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 understand the innards of the JPEG software.
\par 
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 The best short technical introduction to the JPEG compression algorithm is
\par \tab \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 Wallace, Gregory K.  "The JPEG Still Picture Compression Standard",
\par \tab \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 Communications of the ACM, April 1991 (vol. 34 no. 4), pp. 30-44.
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 (Adjacent articles in that issue discuss MPEG motion pi\hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 cture compression,
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 applications of JPEG, and related topics.)  If you don't have the CACM issue
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 handy, a PostScript file containing a revised version of Wallace's article is
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 available at ftp://ftp.uu.net/graphics/jpeg/wallace.ps.gz.  The file (actually
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 a preprint for an article that appeared in IEEE Trans. Consumer Electronics)
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 omits the sample images that appeared in CACM, but it includes corrections
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 and some added material.  Note: the Wallace article is copyright ACM and IEEE,
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 and it may not be used for c\hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 ommercial purposes.
\par 
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 A somewhat less technical, more leisurely introduction to JPEG can be found in
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 "The Data Compression Book" by Mark Nelson and Jean-loup Gailly, published by
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 M&T Books (New York), 2nd ed. 1996, ISBN 1-55851-434-1.  This book provides
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 good explanations and example C code for a multitude of compression methods
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 including JPEG.  It is an excellent source if you are comfortable reading C
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 code but don't know much about data compression in general.  The book's JPEG
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 sample code is far from industrial-strength, but when you are ready to look
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 at a full implementation, you've got one here...
\par 
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 The best full description of JPEG is the textbook "JPEG Still Image Data
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 Compression Standard" by William B. Pennebaker and Joan L. Mitchell, published
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 by Va\hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 n Nostrand Reinhold, 1993, ISBN 0-442-01272-1.  Price US$59.95, 638 pp.
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 The book includes the complete text of the ISO JPEG standards (DIS 10918-1
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 and draft DIS 10918-2).  This is by far the most complete exposition of JPEG
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 in existence, and we highly recommend it.
\par 
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 The JPEG standard itself is not available electronically; you must order a
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 paper copy through ISO or ITU.  (Unless you feel a need to own a certified
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 official copy, we recommend buying the Pennebaker and Mitchell book instead;
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 it's much cheaper \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 and includes a great deal of useful explanatory material.)
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 In the USA, copies of the standard may be ordered from ANSI Sales at (212)
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 642-4900, or from Global Engineering Documents at (800) 854-7179.  (ANSI
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 doesn't take credit card orders, but Global does.)  It's not cheap: as of
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 1992, ANSI was charging $95 for Part 1 and $47 for Part 2, plus 7%
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 shipping/handling.  The standard is divided into two parts, Part 1 being the
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 actual specification, while Part 2 covers compliance testing methods.  Part 1
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 is titled\hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456  "Digital Compression and Coding of Continuous-tone Still Images,
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 Part 1: Requirements and guidelines" and has document numbers ISO/IEC IS
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 10918-1, ITU-T T.81.  Part 2 is titled "Digital Compression and Coding of
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 Continuous-tone Still Images, Part 2: Compliance testing" and has document
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 numbers ISO/IEC IS 10918-2, ITU-T T.83.
\par 
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 Some extensions to the original JPEG standard are defined in JPEG Part 3,
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 a newer ISO standard numbered ISO/IEC IS 10918-3 and ITU-T T.84.  IJG
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 currently does not support any Part 3 extensions.
\par 
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 The JPEG standard does not specify all details of an interchangeable file
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 format.  For the omitted details we follow the "JFIF" conventions, revision
\par \hich\af1456\dbch\af31505\loch\f1456 1.02.  A copy of the JFIF spec is available from:
